<title>USA: Petrobras buys one million bbls Escalante crude.</title>
<headline>Petrobras buys one million bbls Escalante crude.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-06-13</dateline>
<text>
<p>Brazil's state oil company Petrobras bought one million barrels of Argentine Escalante crude from a U.S. equity producer for $4.80-85 under benchmark West Texas Intermediate/Cushing, trade sources said on Friday.</p>
<p>The crude loads at the Argentine port of Bahia Blanca at the end of July.</p>
<p>Escalante has an API gravity of 24.1 degrees and a sulfur content of 0.19 percent.</p>
<p>--Patricia Garip-Bertuol NY Energy Desk ((+1 212 859 1620))</p>
</text>
